WEBVTT

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.150
Ta-da.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.290
I caught this big boy myself.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:14.360
I'll cut him up right away.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.220
Just wait until I make dinner.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:17.730
Okay.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.380
That's standard size.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.380
You're just bitter because 
you didn't catch anything.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.430
I'm not bitter.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.350
You saw what happened, Sakura.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.670
I had a hit, too.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.530
If only...

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.030
If only it hadn't snapped my fishing line...

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.840
Mine was definitely bigger.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.170
Sure, sure.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.740
You know what they say about 
letting the big one get away.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.230
It snapped a PE 7!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.310
It would have been a monster!

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.940
Who cares about PE?

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.720
It would have snapped if it got caught 
on a rock, no matter what PE rating.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.700
Was it really even your 
main line that snapped?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.950
Are you sure you didn't just mess 
up the hook because you're rusty?

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:01.490
How dare you?!

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.120
Hey, Sakura...

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.380
Are you sure you didn't want to 
wear that swimsuit you just got?

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:14.300
Wait, did you guys go swimming today?

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.210
We swam lots.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.270
Kyo-san held me up and taught 
me how to do breast strokes.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.310
W-We're going again, right?

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:25.580
We are, right?

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.480
We're going to be on the 
island for a whole week.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.210
I don't know.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.610
The three of us have to 
prepare for the concert.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.690
We can't spend all our time having fun.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.030
Sorry.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:40.410
You spent so much time 
picking out that swimsuit,

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.220
and we went swimming by ourselves.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:50.290
Kyo-nii said all the swimsuits 
you chose for us were cute.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.710
Yeah?

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.010
That's good to hear.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:34.450
Rematch!

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.480
We're having a rematch!

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.650
A rematch?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.990
I'm going to catch one <i>this</i> big tomorrow!

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.160
<i>This</i> big?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.820
Yeah, <i>this</i> big!

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:51.460
All right, let's catch one <i>this</i> big tomorrow!

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:57.710
We're catching a huge one!

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.640
Deep Sea Prisoner
Monochrome Orchard
HOWLING
Hear the Treasured

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.860
All that's left is the 
venue for the new songs.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.560
Yes?

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.120
Sakura.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.740
Do you have some time right now?

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:16.060
Sure.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.860
Can you come to my room?

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.980
There's something I want to show you.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.420
What do you think?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.340
You went with black, huh?

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:41.830
Yeah.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:46.700
I thought I'd do something 
different from the girls.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:51.600
Do you think it's too precocious?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.540
Not at all.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.730
I don't know how to say it, but I 
think it's stylish. You look good.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:04:59.970
Really?

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.590
Sakura, the bath's ready.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:18.730
Huh?

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.750
What are you guys doing together?

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.450
I was showing Kyo my swimsuit.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.860
He says this would look good on me.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.060
Sakura...

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.180
Yeah?

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:35.330
Let me explain this so 
that you'll understand.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.640
Which would you prefer:

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:41.360
Seeing a picture just of the fish you caught,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.940
or having the fish cooked for you to eat?

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:49.230
Huh?

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:51.200
Eh?

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.710
D-Did I make a mistake?

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:02.020
I guess I need to teach you until you get it.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.550
Sakura, it's time for a lecture.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.900
Sheesh.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.090
Everything is about fishing to you.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:13.310
Isn't there something more important?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:17.310
Looks like lecture time 
is going to take a while.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.390
What's this?

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:24.020
I didn't see this here earlier.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.490
<b>Leave now, or there will be misfortune</b>

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:36.330
What?

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.410
You're not going?

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.380
We're taking a boat to catch red snapper.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.210
You're going to regret not going.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.710
I think I'll pass for today.

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.840
Are you going to watch 
the girls practice, then?

00:06:55.510 --> 00:07:02.340
I want to take a walk in the 
wilderness to find myself.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.820
I wonder if my lecture 
yesterday was too powerful.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.780
I don't mind, but you turning 
down a fishing trip?

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:14.010
It's going to rain. 
It's going to rain cats and dogs.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.330
Did you not sleep well, Sora-chan?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.200
Nah.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.310
She's just...

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.650
<i>You turning down a fishing trip?</i>

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:30.920
<i>It's going to rain. 
It's going to rain cats and dogs.</i>

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:36.450
<i>It can't be, can it?</i>

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:43.490
It's an old building, but you can 
make as much noise as you want here.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.270
You can get plenty of practice.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.110
Thank you very much.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.210
I appreciate it.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:51.030
I'll come pick you guys up before noon.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:56.450
Also, if you wouldn't mind, could you 
come to the shrine with me after lunch?

00:07:57.860 --> 00:08:03.620
We're setting up the stage. 
They want to talk to you about acoustics.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.050
Sure, got it.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.980
It's getting a lot better.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.400
I think this new song's ready for the concert.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:29.540
Why don't we take a short break?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:38.200
My fingers are tired from practicing all day.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.930
Kyo, massage them for me.

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:42.630
No fair, Zomi.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.710
Kyo-san, massage mine, too.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.180
Help me, Kyo-san!

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.290
No!

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:57.120
No!

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.060
I can't see, Nozomi!

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:06.230
Bad boys go outside.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:10.470
Thanks, Sora.

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.350
You're amazing, Ku-chan.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:14.570
I'm so glad you're in my family.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:20.080
I've never been overly afraid of 
bugs, ever since I was born.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:23.330
Thanks for coming out here.

00:09:23.800 --> 00:09:27.880
Nah, it's good to check acoustics early.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:29.840
I'm grateful you asked.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.210
I'm glad you say that.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:35.090
He is in charge of acoustics.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.390
Hey, Manager-san.

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:38.220
Over here.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.180
M-Manager-san?

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:41.180
Um...

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.300
I have to be somewhere.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.730
Can I leave the rest to you?

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:47.890
Yeah, I'll be fine.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:51.270
Would you mind taking a look at the stage?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:52.770
O-Okay.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.720
So for the guitar, should we just pick 
up the amp's output through the mic?

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:00.410
Yes.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.230
I think that'll sound more impressive.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.500
And the bass?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.950
The low-range is harder to pick up,

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:11.670
so it might be better to 
hook up the bass directly,

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.420
and just use the amp as a 
monitor for the bassist.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:20.570
Stop it!

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:24.060
Let go!

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:27.900
Hey!

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.060
Stop!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.060
You're tickling me!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.770
Jun! Nozomi!

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.610
Kyo-san!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.710
Kyo!

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:58.630
Sora!

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.420
Is everyone okay?

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.180
What was that?

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:22.910
Those muntjacs are called John and Smith.

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:27.370
They have an odd habit of trying 
to eat little girls' clothes.

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:30.540
They don't normally show up here.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.690
I wonder why they're here.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.050
I misjudged them.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.550
I thought they'd all be town-bred weaklings.

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:43.410
One of them is a problem.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:49.930
I didn't plan to do anything too terrible, 
but I'm running out of options.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:53.330
Don't blame me, Hibiki.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:12:01.450
Your music will be conveyed 
in the world inside my art.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.470
Tell me if you're itchy anywhere.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.130
My butt.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:22.840
Got it.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:29.680
Full points for service.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.170
We got a lot of help today.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.690
<b>Leave now, or there will be misfortune</b>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.370
Hey, what are you doing?

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.340
Sakura, what's are you...

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.290
Don't worry, Kyo.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.920
I'm just making an immediate arrest.

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.180
Aigae-san?

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.530
Is something wrong?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.790
Those are my picks and spare strings.

00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.580
My strings and picks, too.

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:20.730
My sticks are there, too.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:25.150
I don't know what you think 
you're doing, but this is theft.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.940
Why are you doing this?

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:32.660
I'm sorry.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.460
I saw you when I was out looking for myself.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:40.070
You were on the roof of the cottage.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:46.810
When I heard about the centipede 
later, I thought maybe...

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:51.810
But I hadn't seen you do it, and I didn't 
have any evidence, so I kept quiet.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:55.770
So it <i>was</i> your doing, though.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.350
They don't normally show up here.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.480
I wonder why they're here.

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:05.860
Did you bring John and Smith, too, Aigae-san?

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:11.370
No...

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.540
What should we do, Kyo?

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:18.620
After what she's done, 
we have plenty to make a case.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:24.630
Um, Kyo-san...

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:30.220
If the police come, what's 
going to happen to the concert?

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:32.930
If the police come,

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.380
and they find out that the hosts of 
the event did something like this...

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:37.630
it might get canceled.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:42.270
Then I don't want you to tell the police.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:45.030
I want to do the concert.

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.150
Sora...

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:51.420
I don't get why she would nominate 
us, and then do this to us.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.330
It pisses me off.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:58.710
But the island drummers said they're 
looking forward to our concert together.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.040
I want to do it for them.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:05.030
I don't want to let everyone 
down just because of her.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.480
Yeah, let's do the concert.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:25.360
That's why we're here, after all.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.730
Did you hear that?

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:30.330
Do you feel lucky?

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.490
Or...

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:46.210
This rain seems prohibitive.

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:49.340
The storm's getting close.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.090
It looks like it'll peak past noon.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:58.120
The storm is supposed to pass by tomorrow.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:01.340
We should call off the band practice today.

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:04.920
That cottage is quite run-down.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:22.040
Nozomi, right hand red.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:28.190
Here we go.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:33.170
<b>Left
hand</b>

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.170
Jun, left hand red.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.600
I'm done!

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:49.570
Jun loses.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:52.760
That's ten in a row.

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.450
No, eleven in a row.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:56.860
I don't care.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:58.700
Just get off me!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.190
The wind's getting stronger.

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:05.140
It'll be bad if the stage gets blown away

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:08.770
I hope the bungalow we were 
using for practice is okay.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:13.590
Maybe we should move the drums 
and equipment over here.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:17.590
Centipedes are no threat for the drums,

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.180
but I'm worried about them getting wet.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.570
That's true.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:25.140
I don't think we should keep the 
drums and equipment in the bungalow.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.730
I'll go ask Sayuri-san if I can go get them.

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:32.320
Wait, we'll come with you.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.950
Yellowtail Blue snapper

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.950
<b>Length
Weight</b>

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.950
<b>Ojiro Kenta</b>

00:17:35.350 --> 00:17:36.310
What?

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:38.580
She's not at the community 
center or at school, either?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.590
Then where is she?

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:45.550
Hang on, I'll call you right back.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.840
I'm sorry, I'm going out for a bit.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:52.420
Is something wrong?

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.630
Yuzu-chan is missing.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.630
Aigae-san?

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.660
Yes.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:01.860
Her parents say she snuck out.

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:07.020
I don't think an island girl would do 
anything crazy in this weather, but...

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:10.110
Would it be okay if we helped look for her?

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.270
I can't allow that.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:15.330
The storm will be here sooner 
than you'd expect.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.280
It'll be even more trouble if you get stuck.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:21.160
I understand.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:24.150
But besides that, I need to ask something.

00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:27.660
Could we go to the bungalow 
to pick up our equipment?

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.460
Well...

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.080
That cottage won't fall apart in the 
storm, but I understand your concern,

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.780
not having your precious belongings with you.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:41.410
There'll be enough time for that 
before the windstorm gets really bad.

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:42.590
All right.

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:44.020
Do you have a ride?

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:46.970
Thank you.

00:18:46.970 --> 00:18:49.690
I'll ask Masayoshi-san to take us there.

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:53.850
Promise that you'll be 
back at the lodge before noon.

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:54.900
Got it?

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:55.920
Yes.

00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:57.050
Understood.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.150
Are you worried about the girl?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:17.700
Yeah.

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:19.140
A little.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:30.030
It looks like it hasn't rained through.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:32.210
Thank goodness.

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:34.690
Better safe than sorry, though.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:37.150
Let's hurry up and take it all back.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.170
Yeah.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:41.700
I heard it's going to get even worse by noon.

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:47.200
It'll be bad if my precious 
belongings get taken by the wind.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.390
Precious belongings?

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.460
Kyo, where are you...

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.740
<i>Could she be...</i>

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:07.940
<i>Aigae-san, did you go to protect 
your precious belongings?</i>

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:20.900
Aigae-san.

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:23.200
Nukui-kun.

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:25.510
I thought you'd be here.

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:28.770
I know how you feel, but this is dangerous.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.690
The storm's coming.

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:36.230
You know that better than I do, don't you?

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.530
Still...

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:38.630
Still...

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:41.310
I need to protect this mural.

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:44.250
I messed up.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.720
This is all I can do.

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:51.310
Aigae-san!

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:03.150
Thank you, Yuzuha.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:16.670
It's okay.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:25.870
Who are you?

00:21:25.870 --> 00:21:27.830
Kiryu-sama.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:34.460
This is our first time 
meeting in person, Hibiki.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:38.440
And I'm sorry for lying to you.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.820
Yuzuha isn't Kiriyume.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.950
Kiriyume is actually...

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.250
me.

00:21:51.490 --> 00:21:54.950
<b>Pretty Girl in the Mural</b>

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:41.500
<b>#9: The Grade School Kids Might've Not Been Able to Save the Drowning God if They Hadn't Gotten There in Time</b>

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:32.690
I'm sorry for being out fishing 
all the time when I'm a guardian.

00:23:32.690 --> 00:23:36.180
I regret all the disappointment.

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:39.020
Rained out.
